          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong clique
            in a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a contractible choice of objects, i.e. a collection of objects of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            which are isomorphic to each other in exactly one way.
          %p
            Cliques are ubiquitous in category theory:
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+properties"} universal properties
            define cliques, not single objects; but also because
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherence+theorems"} coherence theorems
            can be easily phrased in terms of cliques.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong clique
            of a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi T
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\colon T \rightarrow C
            out of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28-2%29-groupoid"} (-2)-groupoid
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indiscrete+category"} indiscrete category
            on an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited set
          %p
            Equivalently, a clique is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctor"} anafunctor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \to C
            from the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+category"} trivial category
            = succeed "," do
              %strong anaobject
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            (not anafunctor)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \to C
          %p
            We can form a category
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Clique
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Clique(C)
            whose objects are cliques of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
